# Shell scripts must have LF endings whatever the checkout platform. A CRLF
# script fails on macOS and Linux before it runs a single line, with the
# famously opaque "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M".
*.sh text eol=lf

# Batch and PowerShell are the Windows counterparts and want CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary documents. Without this, core.autocrlf rewrites CR and LF bytes inside
# compressed streams and byte offsets, which silently corrupts the file: the
# committed v5 and v6 corpora already differ from their working copies, and a
# reader recovers them only by rebuilding the cross-reference table.
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pptx binary
*.docx binary
